{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"The tutorial shows how to add Django Debug Toolbar, a commonly used third-party package.","source_span":"This tutorial will show how to add :pypi:`Django Debug Toolbar<django-debug-toolbar>`, a commonly used third-party package."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"Django Debug Toolbar has ranked in the top three most used third-party packages in the Django Developers Survey in recent years.","source_span":"The Django Debug Toolbar has ranked in the top three most used third-party packages in the Django Developers Survey in recent years."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"Django Debug Toolbar is a third-party package maintained by the community organization Django Commons.","source_span":"It's a third-party package that is maintained by the community organization `Django Commons <https://github.com/django-commons>`_."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"Django Debug Toolbar is installed by running 'python -m pip install django-debug-toolbar' within an activated virtual environment.","source_span":"$ python -m pip install django-debug-toolbar"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"Once installed, the DjDT handle appears on the right side of the browser window when browsing to http://localhost:8000/admin/.","source_span":"you should be able to see the DjDT \"handle\" on the right side of the browser window when you browse to ``http://localhost:8000/admin/``."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"Django Debug Toolbar's issue tracker is on GitHub.","source_span":"Django Debug Toolbar’s is `on GitHub <https://github.com/django-commons/django-debug-toolbar/issues>`_."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"Django Packages (djangopackages.org) is a resource for finding third-party Django packages.","source_span":"the fantastic Django resource, `Django Packages <https://djangopackages.org/>`_."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","statement":"Adam Johnson wrote a blog post outlining characteristics that qualify a package as 'well maintained'.","source_span":"`Adam Johnson has a blog post <https://adamj.eu/tech/2021/11/04/the-well-maintained-test/>`_ that outlines a set of characteristics that qualifies a package as \"well maintained\"."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What command installs Django Debug Toolbar, and where should it be run?","answer":"Run `python -m pip install django-debug-toolbar` within an activated virtual environment."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","fact_refs":[2],"question":"Which organization maintains the Django Debug Toolbar package?","answer":"Django Commons, a community organization."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","fact_refs":[1],"question":"How has Django Debug Toolbar ranked in the Django Developers Survey in recent years?","answer":"It has ranked in the top three most used third-party packages."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Where does the DjDT handle appear after installing Django Debug Toolbar and visiting the admin page?","answer":"On the right side of the browser window when browsing to http://localhost:8000/admin/."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","fact_refs":[5],"question":"Where can you find Django Debug Toolbar's issue tracker?","answer":"On GitHub, at the django-commons/django-debug-toolbar repository."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_tutorial08","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What resource is recommended for finding third-party Django packages?","answer":"Django Packages, found at djangopackages.org."}
