{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"Django's documentation contains almost 450,000 words.","source_span":"Django's got a *lot* of documentation -- almost 450,000 words and counting"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"Reading every word of the introductory material amounts to reading about 5% of the overall Django documentation.","source_span":"if you've read every single word, you've read about 5% of the overall documentation"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"Django's documentation is kept in the same source control system as its code, living in the docs directory of the Git repository.","source_span":"Django's documentation is kept in the same source control system as its code. It lives in the :source:`docs` directory of our Git repository."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"The most recent version of the Django documentation lives at https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/.","source_span":"The most recent version of the Django documentation lives at https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"Documentation-related changes, corrections, and suggestions should be submitted via the ticket system at https://code.djangoproject.com/.","source_span":".. _ticket system: https://code.djangoproject.com/"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"For help with a particular Django setup rather than documentation tickets, users should try the Django Forum or the Django Discord server.","source_span":"try the `Django Forum`_ or the `Django Discord server`_ instead."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"The Unix grep utility can be used to search Django's plain-text documentation, e.g. 'grep -r max_length /path/to/django/docs/'.","source_span":"$ grep -r max_length /path/to/django/docs/"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","statement":"Django's documentation uses a system called Sphinx to convert from plain text to HTML.","source_span":"Django's documentation uses a system called Sphinx__ to convert from plain text to HTML."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Roughly how many words does Django's documentation contain?","answer":"Almost 450,000 words."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","fact_refs":[1],"question":"If you read all of Django's introductory material, what percentage of the overall documentation have you covered?","answer":"About 5%."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","fact_refs":[2],"question":"Where is Django's documentation stored, and how is it tracked alongside the code?","answer":"It's kept in the same source control system as the code, in the docs directory of the Git repository."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_whatsnext","fact_refs":[3],"question":"Where does the most recent version of Django's documentation live online?","answer":"At https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/."}
